    "receivedAt": "2026-07-13T10:00:00Z",
    "bodyText": "Estimado equipo de farmacovigilancia,\n\nAdjunto el informe de una paciente que presento una reaccion adversa grave al Neptazol y requirio hospitalizacion. Quedo atenta a cualquier consulta.\n\nSaludos,\nDra. Fernanda Ruiz",
    "status": "PROCESSED",
    "attachments": [
        {
            "id": 11,
            "filename": "icsr-07-es-form.pdf",
            "mimeType": "application/pdf",
            "processable": true,
            "pdfFlavor": "NON_ENGLISH",
            "detectedLanguage": "es",
            "pageCount": 1,
            "processed": true,
            "summary": "This document is an adverse reaction report concerning a 60-year-old female patient who experienced a serious reaction while taking Neptazol, a medication prescribed at a dose of 20 mg once a day orally. The treatment period was from July 5 to July 12, 2026. According to the report from the treating physician, Dr. Fernanda Ruiz from Spain, the patient developed a generalized skin rash and fever on July 11, 2026. The adverse reaction was serious enough to require a one-day hospitalization, although the condition resolved afterward.\n\nGiven the serious nature of the reported adverse event leading to hospitalization, this document is relevant for patient safety reviews. It highlights potential risks associated with the use of Neptazol and indicates the importance of monitoring for adverse reactions in patients receiving this medication. The specifics regarding the onset of the reaction and subsequent medical intervention provide crucial information that could assist in evaluating the medication's safety profile. This report should be reviewed further to assess whether similar cases have occurred and if any regulatory actions are necessary."
        }
    ],
